        ":question/id": "bd6b1200-c721-515b-8eb1-545585b8c043",
        ":question/problem": "Find $f^{′}(x)$ if $f(x) = 23\\tan x - 5x^{5} - \\cot x$.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(23\\tan x-5x^{5}-\\cot x) \\\\ & =23\\sec^{2}x-5\\cdot5x^{4}-(-\\csc^{2}x) \\\\ & =23\\sec^{2}x-25x^{4}+\\csc^{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
